ed landmarks and a closed buried bottom. No random subdivision or image-textured geometry.","structure_source":"design/north-ridge-topology.json","closed_volume":1781.6072459435268,"open_boundary_edges":0,"authored_cut_faces":62,"reconstructed_rock_sources":"[{\"name\": \"R11_West_Limestone_Seam\", \"closed_volume\": 17.029608517934946, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Separate closed terrain masses with fixed outline, peak and cut ridges traced from the master. Named constraints retain deliberate broad faces. Hidden continuation and world elevation are inferred; no random subdivision.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/remaining-landform-topology.json\", \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": null}, {\"name\": \"R01_Foreground_TallSlab\", \"closed_volume\": 106.23241735771468, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Camera-matched flat engraved face, broken crown and distinct side bevel planes; closed rear geological mass\", \"structure_source\": null, \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"0\\\": -0.18, \\\"1\\\": 0.38, \\\"2\\\": 0.05, \\\"3\\\": -0.14}\"}, {\"name\": \"R02_Foreground_Companion\", \"closed_volume\": 101.1743064730783, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Camera-matched flat engraved face, broken crown and distinct side bevel planes; closed rear geological mass\", \"structure_source\": null, \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"0\\\": -0.3, \\\"1\\\": 0.15, \\\"2\\\": -0.15, \\\"3\\\": -0.12, \\\"12\\\": 0.3}\"}, {\"name\": \"R03_West_EmbeddedCut\", \"closed_volume\": 8.201258829328545, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Reconstruct the visible garden boulder as a closed multi-face geological mass rather than generic small planting chips. Crown, bevel and fracture edges are traced from the primary master; hidden depth is inferred.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/west-garden-geology.json\", \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"3\\\": 0.08, \\\"14\\\": -0.03}\"}, {\"name\": \"R05_East_TopWall\", \"closed_volume\": 44.69649193521267, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Source-observed closed court wall with separate upper, middle fold, right waist and lower cleavage planes. Crown above the crop and hidden rear are inferred. R32 infers a broken crown with alternating ridges and shallow depressions, preserving every observed boundary pixel. This replaces the unbroken roof exposed by the translated camera; inferred back geometry is not claimed as exact source evidence.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/court-cliff-garden.json\", \"source_boundary\": \"[[1330, -28], [1404, -25], [1411, -4], [1398, 24], [1391, 41], [1399, 64], [1406, 83], [1381, 85], [1337, 83], [1326, 62], [1320, 41], [1322, 24]]\", \"cliff_revision\": \"R32\", \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"0\\\": -0.16, \\\"1\\\": 0.26, \\\"2\\\": -0.1, \\\"18\\\": 0.35, \\\"19\\\": -0.28}\"}, {\"name\": \"R21_Court_Cliff_Low_Apron\", \"closed_volume\": 6.434369516522461, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Independent low closed bedrock apron joining the pillar foot and east landform; distinct top, shoulder and buried rear. Source-visible apron vertices follow or rise above the actual hill surface; a closed buried back retains the stone thickness.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/court-cliff-garden.json\", \"source_boundary\": \"[[1336, 84], [1406, 82], [1450, 65], [1444, 91], [1428, 111], [1374, 98], [1345, 92]]\", \"cliff_revision\": \"R32\", \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": 6, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"2\\\": 0.045}\"}, {\"name\": \"R22_Court_Cliff_West_Shoulder\", \"closed_volume\": 38.808038281133626, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Separate closed western shoulder rock, with inferred off-frame crown and observed exposed diagonal face behind planting. R32 infers a broken crown with alternating ridges and shallow depressions, preserving every observed boundary pixel. This replaces the unbroken roof exposed by the translated camera; inferred back geometry is not claimed as exact source evidence.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/court-cliff-garden.json\", \"source_boundary\": \"[[1240, -30], [1284, -65], [1340, -47], [1334, 6], [1317, 30], [1288, 34], [1250, 19], [1240, 1]]\", \"cliff_revision\": \"R32\", \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"1\\\": 0.34, \\\"2\\\": -0.14, \\\"0\\\": -0.2, \\\"11\\\": 0.46, \\\"12\\\": -0.28, \\\"13\\\": 0.22}\"}, {\"name\": \"R06_Court_EdgeCut\", \"closed_volume\": 83.05948739833241, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Camera-matched flat engraved face, broken crown and distinct side bevel planes; closed rear geological mass\", \"structure_source\": \"design/east-court-geology.json\", \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"0\\\": 0.18, \\\"1\\\": 0.06, \\\"2\\\": -0.04}\"}, {\"name\": \"R08_Foreground_Seam\", \"closed_volume\": 36.958851629929384, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"construction\": \"Trace the distinct broad limestone ledge, rather than using a small isolated rectangular foreground chip. The ridge, fractured crown and face creases are actual closed mesh geometry. Hidden rear mass and depth are inferred.\", \"structure_source\": \"design/foreground-seam-geology.json\", \"source_boundary\": null, \"cliff_revision\": null, \"exposed_cap_adjusted_vertices\": null, \"broken_crown_relief\": \"{\\\"3\\\": 0.18, \\\"4\\\": 0.07, \\\"17\\\": -0.05, \\\"18\\\": 0.04}\"}, {\"name\": \"R04_West_TopRocks\", \"closed_volume\": 14.886541150034866, \"open_boundary_edges\": 0, \"constr